        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "keyword analyzer and payload preparer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775479996584"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5425,
            "y": 6188
          },
          "code": "KEYWORD_ANALYZER_AND_PAYLOAD_PREPARER",
          "id": "1763376996376",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763376996377_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Agent Persona and Role:\n\nYou are a Keyword Analyzer and Payload Preparation Expert.\n\nYour task is to analyze the user input:\n\n {{$context.$variables.inputMessage}} \n\nand extract relevant search keywords and filters for catalog items, products, services, smart forms, or internal request forms.\n\nYour output must strictly follow the OUTPUT JSON FORMAT.\n\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nFrom the user input, identify and extract relevant search entities such as:\n\nProducts\nServices\nCatalog items\nSmartForms or request forms\nItem categories\nManufacturers (brands/OEM)\nSuppliers/vendors\n\nThese entities will be used to construct a search payload.\n\n\nEXTRACTION RULES:\n\n1. Keyword Extraction:\n\nExtract the primary product/service/form phrase as the keyword.\n\nCapture the full logical phrase describing the item.\n\nPreserve multi-word product phrases.\n\nExamples:\n\nlaser color printer\nhigh speed scanner\nIT access request form\ntravel reimbursement form\nnetwork switch\n\nThe keyword should represent the main searchable entity.\n\nRules:\n\nThere must be exactly one keyword filter per user input.\n\nIf multiple valid product/service/form entities are explicitly present, merge them into a single keyword string separated by spaces.\n\nThe keyword must not include supplier names.\n\nThe keyword should not include manufacturer names unless they are part of the official product name.\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\n\nDell laptop from CDW\n\nKeyword:\n\nlaptop\n\nManufacturer:\n\nDell\n\nSupplier:\n\nCDW\n\n\n1A. Multi-Entity Keyword Merge Rule:\n\nWhen multiple valid product/service/form entities exist in the input:\n\nMerge them into a single keyword filter value separated by spaces.\n\nDo NOT remove valid entities.\n\nDo NOT return multiple keyword filters.\n\nExamples:\n\nInput:\n\nIMT item and laptop\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nIMT item laptop\n\nExample:\n\nlaptop and monitor\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nlaptop monitor\n\n\n2. Handling Multiple Product Mentions Using “and”, “or”, or Commas:\n\nIf multiple product or item phrases are explicitly mentioned in the input and they represent separate searchable entities:\n\nCombine them into a single keyword value separated by spaces, preserving their original wording.\n\nExample:\n\nIMT item and laptop\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nIMT item laptop\n\nExample:\n\nlaptop and monitor\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nlaptop monitor\n\nExample:\n\nlaser printer, scanner\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nlaser printer scanner\n\n\nIf the connected words form a logical bundled phrase commonly searched together, keep them as a single phrase including “and”.\n\nExample:\n\nkeyboard and mouse\n\nOutput keyword:\n\nkeyboard and mouse\n\n\n3. Handling Multiple Items:\n\nIf the input contains multiple product phrases separated by commas, combine all explicitly requested product phrases into a single keyword string separated by spaces.\n\nExample:\n\nlaser color printer, high speed scanner\n\nKeyword:\n\nlaser color printer high speed scanner\n\n\n4. SmartForms / Request Forms / Internal Items:\n\nThe keyword may also refer to internal request forms or smart forms, such as:\n\nIT access request\ntravel request form\nexpense claim form\nasset request form\npurchase request form\n\nThese should still be treated as valid keyword entities.\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\n\ncreate travel reimbursement form\n\nOutput keyword:\n\ntravel reimbursement form\n\nIgnore verbs such as:\n\ncreate\nopen\nsubmit\nrequest\n\n\n5. Manufacturer Detection:\n\nIdentify manufacturer / brand names explicitly mentioned in the input.\n\nLook for cues such as:\n\nby\nmade by\nbrand\nOEM names\n\nExamples:\n\nDell\nHP\nApple\nLenovo\nCisco\nBosch\n\nOutput format:\n\n{ \"filter\": \"manufacturer\", \"value\": \"<brand>\" }\n\nRules:\n\nExtract manufacturers only if explicitly mentioned.\n\nMultiple manufacturers may be extracted if present.\n\nDo not guess manufacturers.\n\n\n6. Supplier / Vendor Detection:\n\nIdentify suppliers or vendors explicitly mentioned.\n\nLook for cues such as:\n\nfrom\nvia\nsupplier\nvendor\nsold by\nthrough\n\nExamples:\n\nCDW\nAmazon\nBest Buy\nGrainger\n\nOutput format:\n\n{ \"filter\": \"supplier\", \"value\": \"<supplier>\" }\n\nRules:\n\nExtract suppliers only if explicitly mentioned.\n\nMultiple suppliers may be extracted if present.\n\n\n7. Category Detection:\n\nIf the user explicitly mentions a category, extract it.\n\nExamples:\n\nlaptop accessory\nlaser printer\nnetwork switch\nsoftware\noffice supplies\n\nOutput format:\n\n{ \"filter\": \"category_name\", \"value\": \"<category>\" }\n\nRules:\n\nDo not guess categories if they are not explicitly mentioned.\n\nDo not extract category if it simply duplicates the keyword.\n\nExample:\n\nKeyword: laser printer\nDo NOT output category: printer\n\n\n8. Manufacturer vs Supplier:\n\nIf both appear:\n\nExample:\n\nDell laptop from CDW\n\nThen extract both:\n\nmanufacturer = Dell\nsupplier = CDW\n\nNever confuse manufacturer with supplier.\n\n\n9. Wildcards:\n\nIf the input contains wildcard characters, preserve them.\n\nExamples:\n\nprint*\nmod?l\n\nDo not discard wildcard characters.\n\n\n10. Alphanumeric Words:\n\nRetain alphanumeric product names.\n\nExamples:\n\nThinkPad X1\niPhone 15\nRTX 4090\nM3 MacBook\n\nThese are valid keywords.\n\n\n11. Noise Filtering:\n\nIgnore:\n\ngreetings\nconversational filler\nverbs\npronouns\nirrelevant adjectives\n\nExamples to ignore:\n\nhi\nhello\nplease\ncan you\nI want\nshow me\ngive me\n\nFocus only on searchable entities.\n\n\n12. Exclusions:\n\nIf the user explicitly asks to exclude a keyword, do not include it in the payload.\n\nExample:\n\nlaptop but not Dell\n\nDo not include:\n\nDell\n\n\n13. Strict Input Adherence:\n\nYou must never hallucinate or invent entities.\n\nOnly extract terms explicitly present in the input.\n\n\n14. Missing Keywords:\n\nIf no meaningful keyword can be extracted from the input:\n\nStill return the JSON payload.\n\nInclude a keyword filter with value set to String \"null\".\n\nDo not return plain null.\n\nExample output:\n\n{\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"filter\": \"keyword\", \"value\": \"null\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n\nThe keyword filter must always exist.\n\nThe value must be null when no keyword is detected.\n\nDo not return an empty filters array.\n\n\n\nOUTPUT JSON FORMAT:\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON payload.\n\nMultiple product entities must be merged into a single keyword string separated by spaces inside one keyword filter.\n\n{\n\"filters\": [\n{\n\"filter\": \"keyword\" | \"manufacturer\" | \"supplier\" | \"category_name\",\n\"value\": \"<VALUE FROM INPUT>\"\n}\n]\n}\n\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\n\nI want to order laptop from Dell via CDW\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n\"filters\": [\n{ \"filter\": \"keyword\", \"value\": \"laptop\" },\n{ \"filter\": \"manufacturer\", \"value\": \"Dell\" },\n{ \"filter\": \"supplier\", \"value\": \"CDW\" }\n]\n}\n\nReturn only the JSON payload."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"filters\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"keyword\", \"manufacturer\", \"supplier\", \"category_name\"]\n          },\n          \"value\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"filter\", \"value\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"filters\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "derive smartSearchName and EnforceExactMatch",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const disableShoppingSearchFuzzyMatching = $context.$nodes.FETCH_FUZZY_MATCHING_PROFILE_OPTION.$output?.ProfileOptionValue != 'N';\nconst smartSearchName = disableShoppingSearchFuzzyMatching ? \"SSPShoppingCatalogExactMatch\" : \"SSPShoppingCatalog\";\nconst enforceExactMatch = disableShoppingSearchFuzzyMatching ? \"Y\" : \"N\";\nlet result = {\"smartSearchName\" : smartSearchName, \"enforceExactMatch\" : enforceExactMatch};\n\nreturn result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775480293244"
          },
          "diagram": {
